  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch02.s07",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch02.s07.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p01.01",
            "text": "Why is a compression method relevant when the goal is to build token vocabularies for language models?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p01.02",
            "text": "Byte pair encoding, or BPE, was introduced in 1994 as a data compression algorithm.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@996",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@999",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1001",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1005",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1007"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p01.03",
            "text": "The core idea is simple: scan the data, find the most common pair of consecutive bytes, replace that pair with a byte that does not occur in the data, and keep doing this iteratively.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1010",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1021",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1024",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1027",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1033",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1037",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1039",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1041"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p01.04",
            "text": "Put another way, the algorithm scans the data from left to right, identifies the byte pairs that occur most often, replaces them with a byte not present in the data, and repeats until no byte pair occurs more than once.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1272",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1274",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1276",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1278",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1280",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1283",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1285",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1287",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1290"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch02.s07.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p02.r01",
            "text": "A concrete sequence makes the mechanics clear.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p02.r02",
            "text": "Take the original data \"a a a b d a a a b a c\".",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1075",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1078",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1081"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p02.r03",
            "text": "When this sequence is scanned from left to right, the most common byte pair is \"AA\".",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1090",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1092",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1098",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1099"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p02.r04",
            "text": "\"AAA\" is not the answer, because a byte pair contains only two consecutive symbols, not three.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1102",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1105",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1107"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p02.r05",
            "text": "In this example, \"AA\" occurs four times.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1110",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1112",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1115",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1117"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p02.r06",
            "text": "The pair \"AA\" is then replaced with \"Z\" because \"Z\" does not occur in the data.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1121",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1124",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1127",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1129",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1133",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1135"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p02.r07",
            "text": "After replacing each occurrence of \"AA\", the new sequence becomes \"z a b d z a b a c\".",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1137",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1140",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1143",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1145",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1148",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1150",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1162",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1165"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch02.s07.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p03.r01",
            "text": "The process then repeats on the compressed sequence.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p03.r02",
            "text": "Looking again for the most frequent byte pair, the example replaces \"AB\" with \"Y\" because \"Y\" does not occur anywhere in the data.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1171",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1173",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1175",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1184",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1186",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1189",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1191",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1194",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1196"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p03.r03",
            "text": "After those replacements, the compressed data is \"z y d z y a\".",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1200",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1202",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1204",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1206"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p03.r04",
            "text": "Replacing common byte pairs with another symbol is called encoding, which is why the method is described as an encoder.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1230",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1232",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1234",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1237"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p03.r05",
            "text": "In the example, \"AC\" appears only once, so it is not encoded further.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1220",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1221",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1224",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1226",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1239",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1241"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p03.r06",
            "text": "The example then replaces \"zy\" with another variable, such as \"w,\" and then stops.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1247",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1249",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1252",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1254",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1255",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1261"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s07.p03.r07",
            "text": "The process stops when no byte pair occurs more than once.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1283",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1285",
              "fKd8s29e-l4@1287"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
